course: dictionary
lesson: 4284
title: Greenfly in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Greenfly are tiny green insects, and the sentences around the word tell you a lot about them. «Ladybirds eat greenfly and help gardens.» Ladybirds are helpful to gardeners, so greenfly must be something gardeners do not want.
explain: Look for clues in brackets too. «Ladybirds, called ladybugs in North America, eat greenfly (aphids) that damage plants, and earthworms keep soil healthy, so gardeners are glad to see them.» The brackets tell you that greenfly are aphids. Try your meaning in the sentence: gardeners are glad to see the ladybirds because they eat the pests that damage plants. That makes sense.
explain: Phrases help too. «Covered in greenfly» and «a plague of greenfly» both describe plants in trouble, and «get rid of greenfly» tells you they are a problem to remove. When a word is new, read the words around it first, and use a dictionary if the clues are not enough.
fact: A greenfly is a tiny green insect, a kind of aphid.
fact: Greenfly suck sap from plants, and this can damage them.
fact: Greenfly often cluster on rose buds and new shoots.
fact: Ladybirds and their larvae eat lots of greenfly, so ladybirds help gardeners.
fact: Greenfly make a sticky liquid called honeydew, which ants like.
exercise: «Ladybirds eat greenfly and help gardens.» Why do gardeners like ladybirds? | Because ladybirds make sticky honeydew | *Because ladybirds eat greenfly that harm plants | Because ladybirds damage rose buds | Because ladybirds are pests
exercise: A rose is «covered in greenfly». What are the greenfly? | A large brown beetle with spots | *A tiny green insect that sucks sap from plants | A kind of tree that grows in gardens
exercise: Find and copy the word in brackets that means the same as greenfly. | plants | *aphids | soil | earthworms
test: What do ants like that greenfly make? | Pollen | Sap | *Honeydew | Soil
test: «Get rid of greenfly» means what? | Plant more roses | Keep them safe on the plants | *Remove them from the plants | Feed them to the ladybirds
exam: Which sentence shows that greenfly harm plants? | Ladybirds eat greenfly and help gardens | *A plague of greenfly covered the new shoots and sucked their sap | Greenfly are very small | Rose buds are pretty
